(* The output the specification DOES require after the fault is reachable.
   Expected: TRUE.

   The guard against a vacuous property. If 03 returns FALSE only because
   nothing at all is reachable after APP_PARTIAL_SUBMISSION, then the oracle
   has nothing to observe and the test case cannot conclude anything. A FALSE
   in 03 is only meaningful alongside a TRUE here: the specification forbids
   SUBMITTED_FG and offers NO_SUBMISSION in its place.
*)
< true* . "APP_PARTIAL_SUBMISSION" .
  (not "SAVE_SUBMISSION !CRS_0 !ASN_0 !PLACEHOLDER")* .
  "SUBMISSION_STATUS !ASN_0 !NO_SUBMISSION" > true
